iian scenery  and culture finding ohana does a great  job of showcasing its breathtaking  vistas and unique cultural components to  make the whole film feel new and  exciting finding ohana is a  family-friendly adventure with just  enough nostalgia and beauty to keep  adults invested alongside a heap of  adventure and goofiness to win over the  kids  that smells like the butthole the hell  unless you happen to live in the british  countryside it's likely that you could  do with a little more scenery like this  in your life throw on a fascinating  period piece and a few fantastic actors  and you have what's probably netflix's  highest profile film of 2021 so far the  dig based on the 2007 novel by john  preston the dig stars ray fines and  carrie mulligan set in the late 1930s  mulligan plays a woman named edith  priddy who hires archaeologist basil  brown to excavate the land around her  property as brown gets further along in  his dig however he realizes that he may  be unearthing the discovery of a  lifetime the dig is one of those movies  that will have history hounds scrambling  once it's finished to learn more about  the true story surrounding it but  despite concerning itself with a  monumental and historic find this is  mostly a character-driven tale mulligan  and finds both give it their all and  many critics have lauded the film's  subdued pacing and moving drama  life is very fleeting  i've learned that  it has moments you should seize  it would be incredibly easy to just  scroll right past space sweepers but if  you're a fan of sci-fi action that would  be a huge mistake this adventure film  has been referred to by several outlets  as korea's first space blockbuster and  it features some great character work a  fun and compelling story and some  surprisingly strong visual effects space  sweepers takes place in a future where  earth is on the verge of being  uninhabitable select wealthy individuals  are given a chance to live on a space  station but most o